<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  A TEMPLATE. NOTHING IN THIS REPOSITORY INSTALLS IT, and no test ever runs `launchctl load` or
  `launchctl bootstrap`. Replace __REPO__ and __HOME__, copy the result to
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.marketplace-deal-finder.collector.plist, and bootstrap it by hand.
  docs/collector-ingest.md carries the four commands.

  StartCalendarInterval, NOT StartInterval, and the keys are NOT interchangeable on a Mac that
  sleeps. man launchd.plist:

    StartInterval -- "If the system is asleep during the time of the next scheduled interval
    firing, THAT INTERVAL WILL BE MISSED due to shortcomings in kqueue(3)."

    StartCalendarInterval -- "Unlike cron which skips job invocations when the computer is
    asleep, LAUNCHD WILL START THE JOB THE NEXT TIME THE COMPUTER WAKES UP. If multiple
    intervals transpire before the computer is woken, those events will be coalesced into one
    event upon wake from sleep."

  So StartCalendarInterval recovers exactly one run on wake where StartInterval silently loses
  the window. DO NOT SWAP THE KEY.

  RunAtLoad is false because the man page says the key "should be avoided, as speculative job
  launches have an adverse effect on system-boot and user-login scenarios". The install runbook
  ends with one manual `launchctl kickstart`, so the operator still gets immediate confirmation.

  NO EnvironmentVariables BLOCK, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THE WRAPPER. Files in
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents are world-readable; COLLECTOR_TOKEN in this file would be a live secret
  in one. scripts/collector-run.sh sources it from ~/.marketplace-collector.env and refuses the
  file unless its mode is 600.

  No ThrottleInterval: the 10 s default floor is irrelevant at 1,800 s.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.marketplace-deal-finder.collector</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__REPO__/scripts/collector-run.sh</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
  </array>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/marketplace-collector.log</string>

  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/marketplace-collector.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
